PATCH 521: the three MGA sprite dispatchers read the position descriptor from a different parameter slot
each, and none of them from the one every caller uses.

FUN_0000_26a1, FUN_0000_279d and FUN_0000_294d are reached ONLY through the [DGROUP:0x6b4] vector -- an
icall, no direct callers -- and their asm is

    26a1: 53 push bx ; 8b 3e 24 07 mov di,[0x724] ; e8 63 ff call 0x260c

so AX (the sprite-directory byte offset) and BX (the position descriptor) arrive LIVE from the paint
handler.  Ghidra's __allregs varnode order placed BX in a DIFFERENT slot for each of them -- 26a1 read
param_4, 279d param_3, 294d param_4 -- while FUN_0000_2ae9 (patch 312) already read param_2.  No single
call shape can satisfy all four, and every [0x6b4] caller in this tree passes (ax, bx): patches 503, 504,
506, 507, 508, 509, 517, 518, 519, 520.  All three now read param_2, uniform with 2ae9.

MEASURED.  With the handlers themselves fixed (patch 517), FUN_0000_787d hands 26a1 ax=0x380 and
bx=0x8eee exactly as the asm says -- and 260c was STILL receiving 0xe515 as its position descriptor,
i.e. param_4, i.e. stack garbage.  A gdb watchpoint on the full write sequence to DGROUP:0x158a inside
tick 274 shows every one of the eight 260c calls in that frame getting its descriptor from the wrong
slot (0xe515, 0x8ef6, 0x3b7c, 0x3b88, 0x3b94, 0xa9fb, 0x8f12, 0x3be8 against the 0x8eee/0x8ef6/... the
handlers actually pass).

This is the native<->wasm RENDER divergence the extended fingerprint reports at t=274 -- the FIRST
in-mission tick -- in 260c's clip outputs DGROUP:0x1586..0x158f, with every simulation block identical.
